                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support><p>Rectangular plaque reconstituted from two contiguous fragments, with break between stoens in upper third. There is a fragment missing from the top right corner, and some wearing on the right hand side below the missing fragment.</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.stone.marble" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html">Marble (Candoglia)</material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.statuebase" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/57.html">Statue Base</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">36</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">40</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">48</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.incomplete"/>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout><p>This inscription lies centered in the middle of entablature. The text takes up almost the entirety of the space assigned to it with little empty space. There are some lines which have parts either missing or damaged on the right hand side, particularly around the missing fragment.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.chiselled" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">chiselled</rs>
                                    <damage/>
                                </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>The handwriting is broad and of a consistent height, however is inconsistent in the angle of the lettering and quite tight in spacing. Most of the inscription is legible, however there is some wear on the remaining sections of the right hand side. Use of triangular interpuncts.</p>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line6">Lines 1–6</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm">23–30</height>
                                </dimensions>
                            </handNote>
